      "id": "aapl-risk-suppliers",
      "type": "narrative",
      "answer": "Apple says it depends on outsourcing partners, mainly in China mainland, India, Japan, South Korea, Taiwan and Vietnam, for component and product manufacturing and logistics, and that it relies on single-source partners for many components and on Asian partners for final assembly of substantially all hardware. It warns that this reduces direct control over production and distribution, which has in the past hurt cost, quality or quantity, and that it remains responsible to consumers for warranty and product defect liabilities. It also states that custom components from single sources, supply shortages (e.g., semiconductors), capacity constraints, and difficulty finding alternative suppliers could materially harm its business, results and stock price (FY2025 10-K).",
      "found": true,
      "value": null,
      "cost_usd": 0.000952,
